id: pm-gh1562
title: "GH-1562: expose calendar matching totals and bounded continuation"
description: "Reported on2026.10.23: runCalendar limit2 returns two of three reminders while exposing only post-limit summaries and filters.limit, with no total, omission receipt, has_more or bounded continuation. Investigate core SDK completeness metadata and recoverable bounded reads, without claiming stored data loss."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: agent-ux,"gh:1562",sdk
created_at: "2026-10-23T15:20:50.258Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T12:38:41.389Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-24T12:38:39.735Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-24T12:38:39.735Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: A limited calendar result discloses matching versus returned scope and omissions; callers can recover omitted rows through bounded continuation or a concrete bounded recovery with stated consistency limits; public CalendarResult types describe the completeness fields; sandboxed reminder and deadline controls cover exact-full and truncated windows without stored data loss.
parent: pm-qh3p
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "CalendarResult now publishes matching/returned/remaining row counts, page offset, has_more and next_cursor. Preserve first-page clock and recurrence boundaries, label summary/day buckets as returned_rows, support after in calendar CLI/MCP, and refuse malformed or changed matching sets."
expected_result: A bounded calendar read distinguishes exact-full from truncated results and retrieves omitted reminder/deadline rows without an unbounded reread or stored data loss.
actual_result: "Direct SDK, calendar CLI and MCP continuation recover every reminder/deadline row with stable relative bounds, page-size changes, exact-full/empty/zero-limit controls and stale-set refusal. Linked calendar suite passes38 tests; the same pre-fix completeness case fails. Packed Node/Bun context continuation and coupled contract regressions pass. Full coverage/static and hosted review remain pending merge gates."
affected_version: 2026.10.23
